  "body": "Deadline sale: Closes on Tuesday 1 December 2026 at 12:00PM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nPerfectly positioned in a family-friendly pocket of the Bays, this home gets so much right. Great schools on your doorstep, parks and walkways within easy reach, cafes nearby, and, above all, it’s a fantastically functional family home (mostly on one easy level) with exceptional outdoor spaces. It's somewhere to settle in and enjoy for years to come, with the scope to think bigger down the track if you wish.\r\n\r\nSet on a generous 673m² freehold corner site, directly opposite St Heliers School, this elevated 1960s home has been thoughtfully updated while retaining the architectural merit of its era. Painted tongue-and-groove ceilings throughout create an airy and fresh sense of space, while the modern open-plan kitchen and dining area form the natural hub of family life today.\r\n\r\nThe dining space is a real highlight, with doors opening onto expansive decks on either side, creating one of the best connections between the home and outdoor living you’ll find. The brand-new eastern deck leads to a lush tropical garden, while the north-facing deck is covered by a substantial louvre system for year-round enjoyment. Follow the sun, entertain or simply relax; spending time outdoors will be very much part of living here.\r\n\r\nInside, four bedrooms and a separate lounge provide plenty of room for family life, all on one easy-care level. Downstairs, a substantial flexible space with plumbing offers options for work, hobbies or additional accommodation for guests, alongside a large double garage with ample storage.\r\n\r\nThe lifestyle benefits of the location are hard to beat with St Heliers School across the road, Glendowie College and Sacred Heart nearby, Riddell Road amenities close at hand and St Heliers Village just down the hill. Dingle Dell's walking tracks and the green open spaces of Churchill Park add to the appeal.\r\n\r\nComfortable and beautifully livable as it stands, the home also offers exciting scope to enhance or explore possibilities of the site over time. With Mixed Housing Urban zoning, generous land and a prime Bays position, there's plenty of potential for the future.",
